### 🟠 D-P2-14 — `TextShaper` destructor leaks the CJK and app-font FT_Faces

**Status:** `SOURCE_VERIFIED`
**File:** `text_shaper.cpp` — `~TextShaper`
**Severity:** P2 (memory leak; for a long-running interpreter that reloads fonts per APK, this accumulates)

**Finding:**
```cpp
TextShaper::~TextShaper() {
    for (auto& kv : hb_fonts_) { hb_font_destroy(...); }
    FT_Face r = ...kFaceRegular...
    FT_Face b = ...kFaceBold...
    FT_Face f = ...kFaceFallback...
    FT_Face e = ...kFaceEmoji...
    FT_Face m = ...kFaceMonospace...
    if (m && m != r && ...) FT_Done_Face(m);
    ...
    if (r) FT_Done_Face(r);
    if (ft_lib_) FT_Done_FreeType(...);
}
```
There is no `FT_Done_Face` for `faces_[kFaceCJK].ft_face` (added in the S78 R-NEW-398 patch) and no iteration over `app_faces_` to destroy the app-registered memory faces. Both leak at destruction.

Additionally, `app_faces_[i].bytes` (the `shared_ptr<vector<uint8_t>>`) is kept alive by the face; `FT_Done_Face` must run before the `shared_ptr` drops, otherwise the face will read freed memory during `FT_Done_Face`'s cleanup. Current code never destroys these faces, so this is a *latent* UAF that would appear if anyone adds the missing `FT_Done_Face` call without also handling the buffer lifetime.

**Fix:**
```cpp
TextShaper::~TextShaper() {
    for (auto& kv : hb_fonts_) if (kv.second) hb_font_destroy(...);
    // app faces first (they hold the byte buffers)
    for (auto& af : app_faces_) {
        if (af.ft_face) FT_Done_Face(reinterpret_cast<FT_Face>(af.ft_face));
        af.ft_face = nullptr;
        // af.bytes kept alive until here — do NOT reset before FT_Done_Face
    }
    // base faces (dedup) — include kFaceCJK
    FT_Face r = ..., b = ..., f = ..., e = ..., m = ..., c = faces_[kFaceCJK].ft_face;
    if (c && c != r && c != b && c != f && c != e && c != m) FT_Done_Face(c);
    if (m && m != r && ...) FT_Done_Face(m);
    ... (existing)
    if (r) FT_Done_Face(r);
    if (ft_lib_) FT_Done_FreeType(...);
}
```

**Reproduction:** run 100 APKs through `TextShaper` in one process (or use `valgrind --leak-check=full`) — observe ~N×2 leaked `FT_Face` allocations (one for CJK, one per registered app font).

**Integration:** isolated to `text_shaper.cpp`.

