### 🟠 D-P2-15 — `ManifestReader::parse_plain_xml` does not parse `<uses-permission>`, `<uses-sdk>`, `<uses-feature>`, `<meta-data>`

**Status:** `SOURCE_VERIFIED`
**File:** `manifest_reader.cpp` — `parse_plain_xml`
**Severity:** P2 (functional gap when plain XML manifests are used — e.g., apktool-decoded APKs, hand-authored test manifests)

**Finding:** The state machine in `parse_plain_xml` handles `manifest`, `application`, `activity`, `intent-filter`, `action`, `category` only. The AXML `process_start_element` handles `uses-permission`, `uses-sdk`, `uses-feature`, `meta-data` (including meta-data capture in F-116). The plain-XML path does not.

Consequence: for plain XML manifests, `result_.permissions`, `result_.min_sdk_version`, `result_.target_sdk_version`, `result_.application_meta_data`, `result_.activity_meta_data` all stay empty even when the manifest declares them. Any caller that relies on these (e.g., `ApplicationContext::getApplicationInfo`, permission model in `checkSelfPermission`) behaves as if the manifest has no permissions and no min-SDK.

**Fix:** add the four missing branches to `parse_plain_xml`:
```cpp
else if (tag_name == "uses-sdk") {
    result_.min_sdk_version = extract_attr("android:minSdkVersion");
    result_.target_sdk_version = extract_attr("android:targetSdkVersion");
}
else if (tag_name == "uses-permission") {
    std::string perm = extract_attr("android:name");
    if (!perm.empty()) result_.permissions.push_back(perm);
}
else if (tag_name == "uses-feature") {
    std::string feat = extract_attr("android:name");
    if (!feat.empty()) result_.uses_features.push_back(feat);
}
else if (tag_name == "meta-data") {
    // application-level vs activity-level by in_activity_
    ... (mirror the AXML process_start_element law)
}
```
Also copy the `application_theme_ref` (F-094) capture so plain-XML callers get the theme.

**Reproduction:** create a plain XML manifest with `<uses-permission android:name="android.permission.INTERNET"/>`, parse it with `ManifestReader`, observe `result.permissions.size() == 0` on the current source.

**Integration:** isolated to `manifest_reader.cpp`; the AXML path is unaffected.

