### 🟡 D-P3-9 — `mutf8::read_sleb128` signed left-shift UB in the i=4 branch

**Status:** `SOURCE_VERIFIED`
**File:** `mutf8.cpp` — `read_sleb128`
**Severity:** P3 (cosmetic; implementation-defined, not exploitable on mainstream compilers)

**Finding:**
```cpp
if (i == 4) {
    if ((byte & 0x80) || (byte & 0x7F) > 0x0F) { ok = false; return 0; }
    value |= static_cast<int32_t>(byte & 0x0F) << 28;
```
`static_cast<int32_t>(byte & 0x0F) << 28` with `byte & 0x0F > 7` produces a `int32_t` result whose top bit is set (e.g., `15 << 28 = 0xF0000000`). In C++17, this is UB; in C++20, well-defined but implementation-defined sign. All mainstream compilers preserve two's-complement bits, but the standard does not guarantee it.

**Fix:**
```cpp
value |= static_cast<int32_t>(static_cast<uint32_t>(byte & 0x0F) << 28);
```
i.e., perform the shift in `uint32_t`, then cast to `int32_t`.

**Integration:** isolated to `mutf8.cpp`.

