### 🟠 D-P2-16 — `dex::read_encoded_value` recursion is unbounded (stack overflow on deeply nested annotations)

**Status:** `SOURCE_VERIFIED`
**File:** `encoded_value.h`
**Severity:** P2 (hostile DEX can force stack overflow)

**Finding:** `VALUE_ARRAY` (0x1c) and `VALUE_ANNOTATION` (0x1d) recurse into `read_encoded_value` once per element. A DEX with 50,000 nested single-element arrays consumes 50,000 stack frames (~4 KB each on x86-64 → 200 MB of stack → overflow). The parser has no depth counter.

**Fix:** add a `depth` parameter:
```cpp
inline bool read_encoded_value(const uint8_t* data, size_t size, size_t& p,
                               EncodedValue& out, int depth = 0) {
    if (depth > 256) return false;   // hostile nesting
    ...
    if (!read_encoded_value(data, size, p, elem, depth + 1)) return false;
```

**Reproduction:** craft a DEX whose static-values section contains 100,000 nested `VALUE_ARRAY` headers; parse; observe stack overflow.

