### 🟠 D-P2-17 — `http_client.cpp` chunked reader allocates the full chunk before the body cap

**Status:** `SOURCE_VERIFIED`
**File:** `http_client.cpp` — `read_chunked`
**Severity:** P2 (server-controlled allocation)

**Finding:**
```cpp
unsigned long chunk = strtoul(sz_line.c_str(), nullptr, 16);
...
out += read_exact(ssl, fd, chunk);      // allocates `chunk` bytes
...
if (out.size() > kMaxBody) break;
```
A malicious server can declare `chunk = 0x7FFFFFFF` (2 GB); `read_exact` calls `out.reserve(1 MB)` then appends, growing to 2 GB before the cap check. The cap is checked **after** the allocation.

**Fix:** clamp the chunk request:
```cpp
size_t want = std::min<size_t>(chunk, kMaxBody - out.size());
out += read_exact(ssl, fd, want);
if (chunk > want) break;   // oversized chunk — stop
```

