### 🟠 D-P2-18 — `SharedPreferences` defaulted move constructor is implicitly deleted (`std::shared_mutex` is non-movable)

**Status:** `SOURCE_VERIFIED`
**File:** `shared_prefs.h`
**Severity:** P2 (latent — any future `std::move` of `SharedPreferences` fails to compile; the `= default` is misleading)

**Finding:**
```cpp
SharedPreferences(SharedPreferences&&) noexcept = default;
SharedPreferences& operator=(SharedPreferences&&) noexcept = default;
```
`std::shared_mutex` is neither copyable nor movable in C++17, so both defaulted special members are implicitly deleted. The header claims move support that does not exist. Current call sites store `std::shared_ptr<SharedPreferences>`, so the compile break is latent — but any future code that moves the object will fail.

**Fix:** remove both `= default` lines and document that `SharedPreferences` is non-movable by design (it owns a mutex). Or wrap the mutex in `std::unique_ptr<std::shared_mutex>` to enable move — but that changes the concurrency model.

