### 🟡 D-P3-14 — `ManifestReader::parse_plain_xml` only handles double-quoted attributes

**Status:** `SOURCE_VERIFIED`
**File:** `manifest_reader.cpp` — `extract_attr`
**Severity:** P3

**Finding:** `tag.find(attr + "=\"")` — single-quoted XML (`android:name='Foo'`) is legal XML and is not matched. Any hand-authored or apktool-modified manifest using single quotes loses its attributes.

**Fix:** try both quote styles:
```cpp
for (char q : {'"', '\''}) {
    std::string search = attr + "=" + q;
    size_t p = tag.find(search);
    if (p != std::string::npos) {
        size_t v0 = p + search.size();
        size_t v1 = tag.find(q, v0);
        if (v1 != std::string::npos) return tag.substr(v0, v1 - v0);
    }
}
```

